:: Nursery encounter - lost toy [bg-nursery]
<h1 class="ptitle">NURSERY</h1>
<br /><br />
/* A young student won't leave for school without a favorite toy. */
<<set _cast = setup.nurseryEncounters.cast()>>
<<if !_cast>>
	<<goto 'Nursery'>>
<<else>>
<<set _carer = _cast.carer>>
<<set _kid = _cast.kid>>
<<set _name = setup.displayName(_carer)>>
<<set _heOrShe = setup.pronounceWhat(_carer)>>
<<set _hisOrHer = setup.pronounceWhos(_carer)>>
<<set _himOrHer = setup.pronounceWho(_carer)>>
<<set _kidHe = setup.pronounceWhat(_kid)>>
<<set _kidHis = setup.pronounceWhos(_kid)>>
<<set _kidHim = setup.pronounceWho(_kid)>>
<<set _own = setup.nurseryEncounters.isOwnChild(_kid)>>
<<set _toy = either('rag doll', 'wooden horse', 'knitted bear', 'stuffed rabbit', 'tin soldier')>>

The school crowd is lining up at the nursery door with their coats half on. One of them isn't moving. <<=_kid.name>> stands in the middle of the room with <<=_kidHis>> arms folded and <<=_kidHis>> chin trembling, while <<=_name>> is down on hands and knees, peering under a cot.
<br /><br />
"I can't go without my <<=_toy>>," <<=_kid.name>> says. "I had it. I had it right here."
<br /><br />
<<sayNpc _carer>>
	I know you did, sweetheart. We'll find it.
<</sayNpc>>
<br />
<<=_name>> sits back on <<=_hisOrHer>> heels and sees you. <<=ucfirst(_heOrShe)>> blows a strand of hair out of <<=_hisOrHer>> face.
<br /><br />
<<sayNpc _carer>>
	It sleeps with <<=_kidHim>> every night, so it can't have gone far, but I've checked all the usual spots. And they all need to be out the door soon.
<</sayNpc>>
<br />

<div id="nce_choices">
	<<link `'Help ' + _himOrHer + ' look for it (Uses some time)'`>>
		<<replace '#nce_choices'>>
			<<set _mins = random(3, 6) * 5>>
			<<addmins _mins>>
			<<run setup.nurseryEncounters.change(_carer, 'happy', 2, 4)>>
			<<run setup.nurseryEncounters.change(_kid, 'happy', 3, 5)>>
			<<run setup.nurseryEncounters.changeBond(_kid, 3, 5)>>
			You take the far side of the room and start pulling back blankets. It takes <<=_mins>> minutes and a good deal of crawling before you find the <<=_toy>> wedged behind a cot against the wall. <<=_kid.name>> lets out a shriek when you hold it up, runs over, and clamps it to <<=_kidHis>> chest.
			<<if _own>>
				<br /><br />
				"<<=setup.npc.mcName(_kid, true)>> found it!" <<=_kidHe>> announces to the whole room. "I told them you would!"
			<</if>>
			<br /><br />
			<<=_name>> gets up off the floor, laughing, and brushes the dust from <<=_hisOrHer>> knees.
			<br /><br />
			<<sayNpc _carer>>
				You're my hero, and I think you're <<=_kid.name>>'s too. Thank you. Not many people would get down on the floor for this.
			<</sayNpc>>
			<br />
			[[Continue|Nursery]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
	<<if setup.cabinInventory.has('plush')>>
		<<link `'Give ' + _kid.name + ' a new plush (Uses 1 plush)'`>>
			<<replace '#nce_choices'>>
				<<run setup.cabinInventory.drop('plush')>>
				<<set $player.nurseryCare.toys += 1>>
				<<run setup.nurseryEncounters.record(null, 'toys', 1)>>
				<<run setup.nurseryEncounters.change(_carer, 'happy', 2, 4)>>
				<<run setup.nurseryEncounters.change(_kid, 'happy', 1, 3)>>
				<<run setup.nurseryEncounters.changeBond(_kid, 1, 3)>>
				You crouch down and hold out a new plush. <<=_kid.name>> takes it with some suspicion, turns it over, and tries a small hug. It isn't the <<=_toy>>, and <<=_kidHe>> makes sure you know it. Still, <<=_kidHe>> tucks it under <<=_kidHis>> arm and goes to join the line.
				<br /><br />
				<<sayNpc _carer>>
					That was kind of you. Thank you. I'll keep looking while they're at school, and now there's one more for the shelf.
				<</sayNpc>>
				<br />
				[[Continue|Nursery]]
				<<nurseryEffects>>
			<</replace>>
		<</link>>
	<<else>>
		<div>Give <<=_kid.name>> a new plush [Need plush]</div>
	<</if>>
	<<link `'Leave ' + _himOrHer + ' to find it'`>>
		<<replace '#nce_choices'>>
			<<run setup.nurseryEncounters.change(_carer, 'happy', -2, -1)>>
			You tell <<=_name>> you're sure it will turn up. <<=ucfirst(_heOrShe)>> looks at the room full of cots, then at the line by the door, and <<=_hisOrHer>> shoulders sag a little.
			<br /><br />
			<<sayNpc _carer>>
				Yes. I'm sure it will. I'll just do it myself, then.
			<</sayNpc>>
			<br />
			<<=ucfirst(_heOrShe)>> ducks back under the cot.
			<br /><br />
			[[Continue|Nursery]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
	<<link `'Tell ' + _kid.name + ' to go to school without it'`>>
		<<replace '#nce_choices'>>
			<<run setup.nurseryEncounters.change(_carer, 'sub', 1, 2)>>
			<<run setup.nurseryEncounters.change(_kid, 'happy', -5, -3)>>
			<<run setup.nurseryEncounters.changeBond(_kid, -5, -3)>>
			You tell <<=_kid.name>> that a toy is no reason to be late, and that <<=_kidHe>> can look for it after class. <<=_name>> opens <<=_hisOrHer>> mouth, catches your eye, and closes it again.
			<br /><br />
			<<sayNpc _carer>>
				You heard. Come on, coat on. It'll still be here when you get back.
			<</sayNpc>>
			<br />
			<<=_kid.name>> says nothing else. <<=ucfirst(_kidHe)>> joins the end of the line with tears running down <<=_kidHis>> face and doesn't look back at you on the way out the door.
			<br /><br />
			[[Continue|Nursery]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
</div>
<</if>>
